      "side": 1,
      "message": "BTW: I just realized this is buggy - I need to re-implement it differently since I am overwriting rsi, which guest doesn\u0027t expect (guest uses `kvm_hypercall2(PKVM_GHC_SHARE_MEM, __pa(addr), size);` and do not expect that rsi is modified (it is not on clobber list of kvm_hypercall2 inline asm) so it can lead to various bugs on guest side.\n\nI could potentially clobber rsi in kvm_hypercall2 but that will not be straight-forward \u0026 hacky + I will need to modify all current guest code, which isn\u0027t practical.\n\n\nI will probably re-implement it by using pkvm_hyp_req-like approach (similar as arm does), which I BTW played with in one of my internal implementation but decided to remove it since considered as too much not needed overhead.\n\nSorry for noise and mistake - I will update this part.",
