      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for reminding about: aosp/3692553 but I think the problem remains:\n1) even with mentioned patch it says that rsi will be input operand so compiler expects it will be read only and not modified by hypervisor so compiler could re-used this value, expecting it is 0 which may not be true after going back from hypervsior. BTW IIUC this problem will actually occur only if the pkvm_set_mem_host_visibility get inlined, otherwise rsi should be preserved by pkvm_set_mem_host_visibility caller due to defined ABI AFIU.\n2) other pVMs basing on other kernel may not have this hypercall implemented similar way as  aosp/3692553\n\nSo I still think it may be buggy and need rework.",
