      "message": "\u003e even with mentioned patch it says that rsi will be input operand so compiler expects it will be read only [...]\n\nOk, yeah, makes sense. (BTW I recall a similar issue observed in the past in real life: aosp/3485324)\n\nRegarding this (independently of the memcache patches):\n\n\u003e other pVMs basing on other kernel may not have this hypercall implemented similar way as aosp/3692553\n\nThis means those pVMs need to be updated to do it similarly to aosp/3692553. The security issue addressed by aosp/3692553 is not specific to Linux guests.\n\nUnless we implement a fine-grained logic in pKVM to decide which registers for which hypercalls to share with the host, which would be more complicated, not scalable, and error-prone.",
